<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>FORM
OF SUBSCRIPTION AGREEMENT</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>LongevityFP
US Large-Cap Fund (1960)</B>&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><I>a
Delaware statutory trust</I></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">This
Subscription Agreement (this &ldquo;Agreement&rdquo;) is entered into by the person or entity identified in the signature pages
(the &ldquo;Investor&rdquo;) and the LongevityFP US Large-Cap Fund (1960), a Delaware statutory trust (the &ldquo;Fund&rdquo;).
Capitalized terms used and not defined in this Agreement have the meanings given to them in the Fund&rsquo;s prospectus, as supplemented
and amended from time to time (the &ldquo;Prospectus&rdquo;).</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>The
Investor should read the Prospectus in full before completing this Agreement. The shares are not suitable for every investor.
The shares are subject to Automatic Cancellation at $0.00 per share upon the death of the associated Reference Life on or after
the Offering Close Date, and an Investor whose associated Reference Life dies before attaining age 80 will receive nothing.</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>PART
I &mdash; SUBSCRIPTION</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>1.&emsp;Subscription.&emsp;</B>The
Investor subscribes for shares of beneficial interest in the Fund (the &ldquo;shares&rdquo;) in the dollar amount set forth in
the signature pages, on the terms of this Agreement, the Prospectus, and the Fund&rsquo;s Amended and Restated Agreement and Declaration
of Trust, as amended from time to time (the &ldquo;Trust Agreement&rdquo;).</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>2.&emsp;Purchase
price; sales load.&emsp;</B>Shares purchased in the initial offering are sold at $10.00 per share. Thereafter, and through the
Offering Close Date, shares are sold at the net asset value per share next determined after acceptance of this Agreement. A front-end
sales load of 7.00% is deducted from the amount subscribed, and the balance is applied to the purchase of shares. The sales load
is waived in full for purchases made through fee-based investment advisory accounts in which the Investor&rsquo;s financial professional
charges an asset-based or financial-planning fee in lieu of transaction-based commissions. No other waiver of the sales load is
available.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>3.&emsp;Minimum
and maximum.&emsp;</B>The minimum investment is $5,000 and the maximum investment is $100,000, applied both per investor and in
the aggregate for all shares associated with any single Reference Life. The Fund will not accept a subscription to the extent
it would cause either limit to be exceeded, and may accept a subscription in part.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>4.&emsp;Irrevocability;
acceptance or rejection.&emsp;</B>This Agreement is irrevocable by the Investor upon delivery to the Fund, subject to any right
the Investor may have under applicable law that cannot be waived. This Agreement constitutes an offer to purchase and is not binding
on the Fund until accepted by the Fund or its agent in writing. The Fund may accept or reject any subscription in whole or in
part, in its sole discretion, for any reason or for no reason, including where the Qualifying Connection documentation is not
provided or is insufficient. If a subscription is rejected in whole or in part, the amount tendered with respect to the rejected
portion will be returned without interest.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>5.&emsp;Payment
and settlement.&emsp;</B>The Investor must deliver the full subscription amount in immediately available funds in the manner specified
in the signature pages. Shares are issued in book-entry form only. No certificates are issued.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>PART
II &mdash; THE REFERENCE LIFE AND THE QUALIFYING CONNECTION</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>6.&emsp;Designation
of the Reference Life.&emsp;</B>The Investor designates in the signature pages one natural person born between January 1, 1960
and December 31, 1960 as the Reference Life associated with the shares purchased under this Agreement. The designation is made
at the time of purchase and may not be changed thereafter for any reason, including a change in the relationship between the Investor
and the Reference Life, a transfer of the shares permitted under Section 17, or the death of the Investor.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif"></FONT></P>

<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 1 -->
    <DIV STYLE="margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1pt solid"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <DIV STYLE="page-break-before: always; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 6pt"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>7.&emsp;Reference
Life information; verification.&emsp;</B>The Investor must provide, and must cause the Reference Life to provide, the Reference
Life&rsquo;s full legal name, date of birth, Social Security number, and third-party reference contacts, for use in the Fund&rsquo;s
survivorship verification. Where the Investor is not the Reference Life, the Reference Life must execute the Reference Life Consent
attached as Exhibit A, and the Fund will not accept this Agreement without it. Where the Investor is the Reference Life, the Investor
gives the consents set out in Exhibit A by executing this Agreement, and no separate Exhibit A is required.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>8.&emsp;Qualifying
Connection; documentation.&emsp;</B>The Investor must have a Qualifying Connection to the Reference Life at the time the shares
are purchased. As part of the subscription process, the Investor must provide affirmative documentation of the Qualifying Connection
satisfactory to the Adviser. The Qualifying Connection is determined as of the time of purchase and need not continue to exist
afterward; a later change in the relationship does not affect the shares or the Reference Life designation.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
purposes of this Agreement, a &ldquo;Qualifying Connection&rdquo; means that the Investor:</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(i)
is the Reference Life;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(ii)
is the spouse or domestic partner, or a parent, child, grandparent, grandchild, or sibling, of the Reference Life, or is otherwise
related to the Reference Life by blood or by law in a manner that gives rise to a substantial interest engendered by love and
affection, or has a lawful and substantial economic interest in the continued life of the Reference Life; or</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(iii)
is a trust, limited liability company, partnership, or other entity or arrangement that is established or maintained for the benefit
of, or that itself has a lawful and substantial economic interest in the continued life of, the Reference Life or one or more
persons described in clause (ii).</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Control
of an entity, without such a beneficial or economic interest, does not by itself establish a Qualifying Connection.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>PART
III &mdash; REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES OF THE INVESTOR</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Investor represents and warrants to the Fund, as of the date this Agreement is delivered and as of the date it is accepted, as
follows.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>9.&emsp;Capacity
and authority.&emsp;</B>The Investor has full power and authority to enter into this Agreement and to perform its obligations
under it. If the Investor is an entity, it is duly organized and validly existing, the person executing this Agreement is authorized
to do so, and the Investor has provided the Fund with documentation of that authority.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>10.&emsp;Qualifying
Connection.&emsp;</B>The Investor has a Qualifying Connection to the designated Reference Life, and identifies in the signature
pages the clause of the definition on which the Qualifying Connection rests. The documentation the Investor has provided in support
of the Qualifying Connection is complete and accurate.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>11.&emsp;Investor
representation.&emsp;</B>The Investor has read the Prospectus, understands the risks of an investment in the Fund, including the
risk of losing the entire investment, and has other assets and income sufficient to meet the Investor&rsquo;s needs without relying
on the investment in the Fund. This representation is made at each purchase. The Fund does not verify this representation and
is entitled to rely on it. The Fund may reject any subscription as provided in Section 4. This representation is a condition to
purchase; it does not affect the shares once issued, and an inaccurate representation under this Section 11 does not cause an
Automatic Cancellation and is not a Qualifying Connection Breach.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>12.&emsp;Eligibility
and residency.&emsp;</B>The Investor is a resident of the state or jurisdiction identified in the signature pages. The Investor
understands that the Fund does not offer or sell shares, and will not accept subscriptions, in any state or jurisdiction in which
the offer or sale would violate applicable insurance, anti-tontine, insurable-interest, or other law, and that the Fund does not
accept subscriptions from residents of Louisiana.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif"></FONT></P>

<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 2 -->
    <DIV STYLE="margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1pt solid"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <DIV STYLE="page-break-before: always; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 6pt"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>13.&emsp;Receipt
of the Prospectus; no other reliance.&emsp;</B>The Investor has received and read the Prospectus, has had the opportunity to ask
questions of the Fund and to obtain the Statement of Additional Information without charge, and is not relying on any representation,
illustration, projection, or statement concerning the Fund other than those contained in the Prospectus. No person has represented
to the Investor that the shares are insurance, an annuity, or a guaranteed instrument, or that any amount is guaranteed or assured.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>14.&emsp;Source
of funds; tax certification.&emsp;</B>The funds used to purchase the shares are the Investor&rsquo;s own and are not derived from
any unlawful activity, and the Investor will provide such information as the Fund or its agents reasonably request to comply with
applicable anti-money-laundering and customer-identification requirements. The Investor has furnished a properly completed and
executed IRS Form W-9 or applicable Form W-8.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>PART
IV &mdash; AGREEMENT TO THE TERMS OF THE SHARES</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>15.&emsp;Automatic
Cancellation &mdash; bargained-for term.&emsp;</B>The Investor agrees, as a bargained-for term of the shares and as a condition
of purchasing them, that from and after the Offering Close Date each share is subject to cancellation at $0.00 per share in accordance
with its terms, as set forth in Article X of the Trust Agreement: if the Adviser determines that the associated Reference Life
has died (including a death during the Offering Period, if the share is then still outstanding), the share is canceled at $0.00
per share on the next annual cancellation date provided for in the Trust Agreement (the &ldquo;Automatic Cancellation&rdquo;).
The Fund pays no consideration and acquires nothing upon an Automatic Cancellation. No amount is payable in respect of canceled
shares except for any annual survival-contingent distribution that vested but remained unpaid as of the date of cancellation.
The Automatic Cancellation is a term of the shares themselves and operates independently of any tender offer.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>16.&emsp;Qualifying
Connection Breach.&emsp;</B>A &ldquo;Qualifying Connection Breach&rdquo; occurs only if (i) in the case of a representation that
the Investor is the Reference Life, or of a relationship described in clause (ii) of the definition of Qualifying Connection,
the representation was untrue when made; or (ii) in the case of a representation resting on a lawful and substantial economic
interest in the continued life of the Reference Life, or on an entity&rsquo;s beneficial or economic interest described in clause
(iii) of that definition, the representation was untrue when made and was made with knowledge of its untruth or without a reasonable
basis. No Qualifying Connection Breach occurs if a Qualifying Connection in fact existed at the time of purchase under any clause
of the definition, regardless of the clause the Investor represented.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Before
a determination of a Qualifying Connection Breach becomes effective, the Fund will give the Investor written notice describing
the basis for the proposed determination and not less than 30 days to respond and to provide documentation, and the determination
must be approved by the Board, including a majority of the Trustees who are not &ldquo;interested persons&rdquo; of the Fund within
the meaning of the Investment Company Act of 1940 (the &ldquo;1940 Act&rdquo;).</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Investor agrees, as a bargained-for term of the shares, that upon a Qualifying Connection Breach the associated Reference Life
is treated, for purposes of the Automatic Cancellation, as having died, and the associated shares are Automatically Canceled at
$0.00 per share. That consequence operates as the same self-executing lapse described in Section 15 and is not a repurchase, redemption,
or a charge assessed against the Investor. A determination may be made at any time, including in connection with the comprehensive
survivorship review conducted before any annual survival-contingent distribution, and may therefore occur many years after the
shares were purchased.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>17.&emsp;Transfer
restrictions; illiquidity.&emsp;</B>The Investor agrees that the shares may not be transferred, assigned, pledged, or otherwise
disposed of, except (i) to the Investor&rsquo;s successor upon the death of the Investor where the Reference Life is still living,
subject to the Fund&rsquo;s verification requirements and the Trust Agreement, and (ii) as approved by the Board in its sole discretion
in extraordinary circumstances. The shares are not listed on any exchange, no secondary market exists or is expected to develop,
and the shares are not redeemable at the option of the Investor. During the Offering Period only, the Fund expects to conduct
tender offers under the Tender Offer Policy at net asset value per share less the 2.00% Repurchase Fee; the Tender Offer Policy
is a policy of the Board, may be modified, suspended, or terminated at any time, and creates no contractual right to tender. No
tender offers are conducted after the Offering Close Date, and shares that have been Automatically Canceled are not eligible to
be tendered.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif"></FONT></P>

